  "description": "KEBROA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C49 H69 Dy3 N10 O7 S4,3(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.521-3.530 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.83-97.33°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy3L(μ3-OH)2(SCN)4(H2O)2]·3MeOH·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
